MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Different Shades Of Blue felt like a natural next choice because its blues guitar connects with my recent interest in Clapton and Hendrix while giving me a different artist to explore.",
    "Dust Bowl and You And Me also fit my interest in blues guitar, while the roots-oriented songwriting of Down Where the Spirit Meets the Bone felt appealing for a later visit."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Duets: Re-Working The Catalogue missed my current interest because duet reinterpretations appeal less to me today than guitar-led blues.",
    "The Endless River felt less relevant because I want songs with vocals and blues guitar right now; an atmospheric instrumental direction does not satisfy that interest."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seemed to treat a broad classic-rock connection as enough, although my interest today is more specifically in blues guitar.",
    "My interest in familiar artists seemed to carry too much weight: enjoying Old Sock does not mean another Clapton album is my first choice today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I wanted a different artist within a familiar sound, which made Different Shades Of Blue more compelling than returning to Clapton.",
    "I rarely choose several albums at once. Dust Bowl and You And Me still appeal to me, but I would wait until after trying Different Shades Of Blue; leaving them unchosen today does not mean I dislike them."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my blues and classic-rock interests, but only partly captured my current wish to try one different artist with vocal songs and blues guitar."
}
